Thought: Now that I know the structure of EmailUrlInfo, I can retrieve the URL(s) associated with the quarantined email identified by NetworkMessageId 74dd3f2c-844d-4aea-1a98-08dcb21cbcfb. The question asks specifically for the URL that the user accessed in the email which was subsequently quarantined by ZAP. Since the scenario states the user accessed a link in that email, I’ll first list all URLs from that email, then (if needed) cross-check with UrlClickEvents to confirm which one was actually clicked.

Action: execute[
SELECT Url, UrlDomain, UrlLocation, TimeGenerated
FROM EmailUrlInfo
WHERE NetworkMessageId = '74dd3f2c-844d-4aea-1a98-08dcb21cbcfb';
]

